{"parentUuid":"19769228-76c8-40d9-abb5-a9024598c1ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FRx5uevtFmEvVMkPjS5CQF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now read the actual ingestion path end to end. Here's where it stands and what I think, grounded in your code.\n\n## Where ingestion is today\n\n1. **Parse:** [extraction.py](runtime/benny/core/extraction.py) runs Docling (PyPdfium backend) with `do_table_structure=True` but `do_ocr=False`, and immediately flattens to markdown via `export_to_markdown()`. Tables survive as markdown tables; **every figure, diagram, chart and photo is dropped on the floor** — the picture elements never make it into the markdown.\n2. **Promote:** [etl_routes.py](runtime/benny/api/etl_routes.py) `promote_staged_files()` is the idempotent staging→`data_in` step (hash/mtime guarded).\n3. **Synthesize:** [synthesis/engine.py](runtime/benny/synthesis/engine.py) chunks the markdown into sections → `parallel_extract_triples` → LLM emits XML triples → Neo4j graph + nomic embeddings (the Chroma split you fixed).\n4. **Route:** [models.py](runtime/benny/core/models.py) `call_model()` is local-first, role-based (`graph_synthesis`), with the thinking-suppression profiles. **Critically: every message content is a plain string — there is no multimodal path.** lmstudio (1234) is already registered; there's no vision model and no `vision` role.\n\nSo the substrate is good, but the pipeline is text-only and visually blind. Your instinct is right.\n\n## The one distinction I'd nail before planning\n\nThere are **two different \"vision RAG\" philosophies**, and PixelRAG is the *opposite* one from what most of your description assumes:\n\n- **Strategy A — Vision-augmented parsing (what you described):** use a VLM to turn each visual element into a *textual surrogate* (caption / mermaid / JSON), stitch those back into the document in reading order, then feed the enriched text into your **existing** triple + embedding pipeline. The knowledge graph stays the source of truth.\n- **Strategy B — Vision-native retrieval (PixelRAG / ColPali / ColQwen family):** skip text extraction, embed **page images directly** with the vision model, retrieve whole pages by visual+semantic similarity, and hand page crops to the VLM at query time. Different index, different retrieval, no intermediate text.\n\nMy strong recommendation: **build A as the foundation** — it plugs straight into the graph + Chroma you already repaired and gives agents structured, inspectable artifacts (a mermaid diagram is something an agent can *read and even edit*). Treat B as an optional **second retrieval lane** later for layout-heavy docs where parsing loses too much. Don't conflate them; they're additive, not either/or.\n\n## On your routing idea — endorse, with refinements\n\nYour \"illustration→describe, diagram→diagram-as-code, table→JSON\" routing is exactly the right shape. Four things it needs to actually work:\n\n1. **A classification step before routing.** \"Is this a decorative illustration or a technical diagram?\" is itself a decision. Docling already tags element *type* (table/picture/formula/code) and gives bounding boxes — but picture *sub-type* (photo vs flowchart vs chart) needs either a cheap classifier or a VLM routing prompt. Don't assume; classify.\n2. **Stitch surrogates back *in place*.** A diagram's meaning depends on the section around it. The surrogate (mermaid/JSON/caption) must replace the element at its original reading-order position, not get appended as an appendix — otherwise triple extraction loses the context that makes it useful.\n3. **Validate every generated artifact.** This is where your memory already bit you (`memo_ray_token_audit` / \"hollow success\"). Mermaid/PlantUML must actually *parse*; chart JSON must validate against a schema. On failure, fall back to a plain text description rather than poisoning the graph with broken code.\n4. **Provenance per element.** Each surrogate keeps page + bbox + an image crop, so a graph node can cite \"Figure 3, p.12\" and the UI can show the crop. This is also what makes the \"multi-model aggregate\" trustworthy — you can always trace a triple back to the pixels it came from.\n\nAnd reframe \"multi-model aggregate\": it's a **router + escalation ladder**, not everything-through-everything. Cheap text/Docling pass first → VLM only on elements that need it → optional second-model *verify* on high-value extractions (tables, diagrams). The \"aggregate\" is the enriched document, not a literal merge of model outputs.\n\n## The hard part (be clear-eyed about it)\n\nThe biggest code surface is **multimodal `call_model`**. Today `messages[].content` is a string everywhere ([engine.py:295](runtime/benny/synthesis/engine.py), [models.py](runtime/benny/core/models.py)). Sending an image means content becomes a list of `{type:\"text\"}` / `{type:\"image_url\", ...}` blocks, and the **local executor short-circuit** (models.py §5) currently pulls `user_msg` out as a string — it would silently drop images. So a real vision call path has to thread through both the LiteLLM branch *and* the local-executor branch. That, plus a `vision` role and a qwen3vl registry entry, is Phase 1 and it's the riskiest plumbing. Worth proving with a single image round-trip before building anything on top.\n\n(Note: `qwen3vl-it-4b-FLM` implies a FastFlowLM/Lemonade build. Verify it actually exposes vision over the OpenAI-compatible `/chat/completions` with `image_url` blocks — some FLM builds are text-only. lmstudio is the safer first target since it's already registered and reliably does vision.)\n\n## Proposed phased plan\n\n- **Phase 0 — Structured DocModel (no VLM).** Stop flattening to markdown immediately. Keep Docling's element tree: types, bboxes, page images, reading order. Export tables to JSON now. Emit an intermediate `*.docmodel.json` in staging. *This improves things on its own and de-risks everything after.*\n- **Phase 1 — Vision plumbing.** Multimodal `call_model`/local_executor; register qwen3vl + a `vision` role; prove an image→text round-trip against lmstudio (then FLM).\n- **Phase 2 — Classifier + describers.** Sub-classify pictures; route to describers (illustration→caption, diagram→mermaid/plantuml, chart→JSON+desc); validate, cache by element content-hash, attach provenance; stitch surrogates back in reading order → enriched doc.\n- **Phase 3 — Graph + retrieval integration.** Feed enriched doc through existing triple extraction; add element-typed chunks to Chroma with type + provenance metadata so agents can query \"the architecture diagrams\"; nodes cite figures.\n- **Phase 4 (optional) — PixelRAG lane.** Page-image embeddings as a parallel retrieval index for layout-heavy docs; VLM-at-query-time.\n\nCaching and an opt-in-per-document flag matter throughout — VLM passes are slow on local NPU/CPU, so the vision pass must be idempotent like `promote_staged_files` already is.\n\nA couple of forks will shape how I write this up:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41703,"cache_read_input_tokens":45018,"output_tokens":7223,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":7223,"cache_read_input_tokens":45018,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcVsjgU7kgjU7EoPFst8X","type":"assistant","uuid":"53e07783-879c-4ce4-be07-19f912923fe7","timestamp":"2026-06-28T15:15:33.649Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"8a533f4f-52c1-4883-9f06-