{"parentUuid":"4303ecde-0d43-4e57-98d2-a1149528cd27","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"76000644-3315-41ac-95ed-c508ea0016f3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014qUhvJcCN6WVM2bxHc8dwz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PIX-001 — Requirements (Normative)\n2\t\n3\tEvery requirement has a unique ID and a one-sentence success criterion. A phase\n4\tis not done until every acceptance row for that phase is `PASS` with evidence\n5\t(see [acceptance_matrix.md](acceptance_matrix.md)).\n6\t\n7\tKeywords MUST / SHOULD / MAY per RFC 2119.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## 1. Scope\n12\t\n13\tIn scope: a vectorless PageIndex spine — tree build, graph load, deterministic\n14\ttriple fan-out, section provenance, cross-document candidate linking, and a\n15\tsingle-call `structured` retrieval route.\n16\t\n17\tOut of scope (this phase): retiring vector RAG; agentic multi-hop tree\n18\ttraversal; OCR/layout extraction changes (reuse existing `extract_structured_text`).\n19\t\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t## 2. Actors\n23\t\n24\t- **Operator (human)** — ingests documents; reads the indexed abstract graph.\n25\t- **Coordinator agent** — reads the abstract, dispatches extractors per section.\n26\t- **Extractor agent** — extracts triples from one leaf section.\n27\t- **Deterministic core** — `call_model()`, lineage, manifest signing, Neo4j.\n28\t\n29\t---\n30\t\n31\t## 3. Functional requirements\n32\t\n33\t### Phase 0 — Pure spine (shipped with ADR-002)\n34\t\n35\t- **PIX-F1** — `flatten_leaves(tree)` MUST return every text-bearing leaf with\n36\t  **no truncation cap**; the whole document is covered.\n37\t- **PIX-F2** — `tree_to_sections(tree)` MUST emit `{node_id, title, text}` per\n38\t  leaf (the `parallel_extract_triples` shape) so triple provenance survives the\n39\t  hand-off.\n40\t- **PIX-F3** — The leaf partition MUST be deterministic: same tree → identical\n41\t  section ordering on repeat.\n42\t- **PIX-F4** — `abstract_outline(tree)` MUST contain titles + summaries only and\n43\t  MUST NOT contain leaf body text.\n44\t- **PIX-F5** — `build_section_edges(doc, tree)` MUST produce a fully connected\n45\t  `(:Document)-[:HAS_SECTION]->(:Section)` hierarchy with no orphan nodes.\n46\t- **PIX-F6** — `validate_tree(tree)` MUST flag missing and duplicate `node_id`s\n47\t  (provenance keys must be unique) and pass a well-formed tree.\n48\t\n49\t### Phase 1 — Tree build at ingest\n50\t\n51\t- **PIX-F7** — A builder MUST turn extracted document text into a `TreeNode`\n52\t  tree **only** via `call_model()` (no direct provider SDK), at temperature 0.\n53\t- **PIX-F8** — The tree MUST persist to `workspace/.benny/pageindex/<source>.json`\n54\t  using workspace path helpers (no absolute paths).\n55\t- **PIX-F9** — `/rag/ingest` MUST accept a `strategy: \"vectorless\"` (or\n56\t  equivalent flag) that triggers tree build; default behaviour is unchanged.\n57\t\n58\t### Phase 2 — Deterministic fan-out + Section graph\n59\t\n60\t- **PIX-F10** — Triple extraction MUST fan out over `tree_to_sections(tree)`\n61\t  instead of `chunks[:10]`.\n62\t- **PIX-F11** — Each persisted triple MUST be anchored to its `Section`\n63\t  (`node_id` + page range), not only to a filename.\n64\t- **PIX-F12** — Section nodes MUST be written to Neo4j as the\n65\t  `build_section_edges` payload describes.\n66\t\n67\t### Phase 3 — Cross-document linking\n68\t\n69\t- **PIX-F13** — A pass MUST propose candidate `Section`↔`Section` links across\n70\t  documents from section **summaries** (abstract layer) before any full-text\n71\t  call.\n72\t\n73\t### Phase 4 — `structured` retrieval route\n74\t\n75\t- **PIX-F14** — The Adaptive RAG router MUST support a `structured` route that\n76\t  performs a **single** node-selection call over `abstract_outline`, then loads\n77\t  the selected leaves for generation (no N-hop traversal).\n78\t\n79\t---\n80\t\n81\t## 4. Non-functional targets\n82\t\n83\t- **PIX-NFR1** — The spine module (`pageindex.py`) MUST import and run with **no\n84\t  LLM and no Neo4j**; its tests MUST pass under `BENNY_OFFLINE=1`.\n85\t- **PIX-NFR2** — `structured` retrieval MUST stay within **two** LLM round-trips\n86\t  (select + generate) to respect the local-NPU latency budget (ADR-002 §4).\n87\t- **PIX-NFR3** — Tree build MUST be reproducible: same input text + same model +\n88\t  temperature 0 → identical tree (byte-equal JSON) on the replay fixture.\n89\t- **PIX-NFR4** — New modules MUST meet the ≥ 85 % coverage release gate.\n90\t- **PIX-NFR5** — No new absolute-path violations (SR-1 ratchet).\n91\t\n92\t---\n93\t\n94\t## 5. Security / governance\n95\t\n96\t- **PIX-SEC1** — Tree JSON and Section writes MUST emit triple lineage\n97\t  (`process/skill/data`) like any other authored artefact.\n98\t- **PIX-SEC2** — Persistence MUST reject path traversal outside\n99\t  `workspace/.benny/pageindex/`.\n100\t\n101\t---\n102\t\n103\t## 6. Open questions (must be resolved before the owning phase merges)\n104\t\n105\t- **OQ-1** (Phase 1) — Tree-builder model + per-node token budget under offline\n106\t  mode (local reasoning model vs. cloud).\n107\t- **OQ-2** (Phase 2) — `Section` schema reconciliation with existing\n108\t  `Concept`/`Document` nodes and the `CORRELATES_WITH` enrichment overlay.\n109\t- **OQ-3** (Phase 3) — Cross-doc candidate-link mechanism on summaries:\n110\t  reasoning call vs. cheap clustering, and the threshold.\n111\t- **OQ-4** (Phase 1) — Trigger: auto-detect structured docs vs. explicit\n112\t  `strategy: \"vectorless\"` ingest flag.\n113\t"}]},"uuid":"af9d4fe6-94c5-4db7-a3c7-6c14a3e41dd4","timestamp":"2026-06-28T15:20:12.089Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime\\docs\\requirements\\12\\requirement.md","content":"# PIX-001 — Requirements (Normative)\n\nEvery requirement has a unique ID and a one-sentence success criterion. A phase\nis not done until every acceptance row for that phase is `PASS` with evidence\n(see [acceptance_matrix.md](acceptance_matrix.md)).\n\nKeywords MUST / SHOULD / MAY per RFC 2119.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nIn scope: a vectorless PageIndex spine — tree build, graph load, deterministic\ntriple fan-out, section provenance, cross-document candidate linking, and a\nsingle-call `structured` retrieval route.\n\nOut of scope (this phase): retiring vector RAG; agentic multi-hop tree\ntraversal; OCR/layout extraction changes (reuse existing `extract_structured_text`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Actors\n\n- **Operator (human)** — ingests documents; reads the indexed abstract graph.\n- **Coordinator agent** — reads the abstract, dispatches extractors per section.\n- **Extractor agent** — extracts triples from one leaf section.\n- **Deterministic core** — `call_model()`, lineage, manifest signing, Neo4j.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Functional requirements\n\n### Phase 0 — Pure spine (shipped with ADR-002)\n\n- **PIX-F1** — `flatten_leaves(tree)` MUST return every text-bearing leaf with\n  **no truncation cap**; the whole document is covered.\n- **PIX-F2** — `tree_to_sections(tree)` MUST emit `{node_id, title, text}` per\n  leaf (the `parallel_extract_triples` shape) so triple provenance survives the\n  hand-off.\n- **PIX-F3** — The leaf partition MUST be deterministic: same tree → identical\n  section ordering on repeat.\n- **PIX-F4** — `abstract_outline(tree)` MUST contain titles + summaries only and\n  MUST NOT contain leaf body text.\n- **PIX-F5** — `build_section_edges(doc, tree)` MUST produce a fully connected\n  `(:Document)-[:HAS_SECTION]->(:Section)` hierarchy with no orphan nodes.\n- **PIX-F6** — `validate_tree(tree)` MUST flag missing and duplicate `node_id`s\n  (provenance keys must be unique) and pass a well-formed tree.\n\n### Phase 1 — Tree build at ingest\n\n- **PIX-F7** — A builder MUST turn extracted document text into a `TreeNode`\n  tree **only** via `call_model()` (no direct provider SDK), at temperature 0.\n- **PIX-F8** — The tree MUST persist to `workspace/.benny/pageindex/<source>.json`\n  using workspace path helpers (no absolute paths).\n- **PIX-F9** — `/rag/ingest` MUST accept a `strategy: \"vectorless\"` (or\n  equivalent flag) that triggers tree build; default behaviour is unchanged.\n\n### Phase 2 — Deterministic fan-out + Section graph\n\n- **PIX-F10** — Triple extraction MUST fan out over `tree_to_sections(tree)`\n  instead of `chunks[:10]`.\n- **PIX-F11** — Each persisted triple MUST be anchored to its `Section`\n  (`node_id` + page range), not only to a filename.\n- **PIX-F12** — Section nodes MUST be written to Neo4j as the\n  `build_section_edges` payload describes.\n\n### Phase 3 — Cross-document linking\n\n- **PIX-F13** — A pass MUST propose candidate `Section`↔`Section` links across\n  documents from section **summaries** (abstract layer) before any full-text\n  call.\n\n### Phase 4 — `structured` retrieval route\n\n- **PIX-F14** — The Adaptive RAG router MUST support a `structured` route that\n  performs a **single** node-selection call over `abstract_outline`, then loads\n  the selected leaves for generation (no N-hop traversal).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Non-functional targets\n\n- **PIX-NFR1** — The spine module (`pageindex.py`) MUST import and run with **no\n  LLM and no Neo4j**; its tests MUST pass under `BENNY_OFFLINE=1`.\n- **PIX-NFR2** — `structured` retrieval MUST stay within **two** LLM round-trips\n  (select + generate) to respect the local-NPU latency budget (ADR-002 §4).\n- **PIX-NFR3** — Tree build MUST be reproducible: same input text + same model +\n  temperature 0 → identical tree (byte-equal JSON) on the replay fixture.\n- **PIX-NFR4** — New modules MUST meet the ≥ 85 % coverage release gate.\n- **PIX-NFR5** — No new absolute-path violations (SR-1 ratchet).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Security / governance\n\n- **PIX-SEC1** — Tree JSON and Section writes MUST emit triple lineage\n  (`process/skill/data`) like any other authored artefact.\n- **PIX-SEC2** — Persistence MUST reject path traversal outside\n  `workspace/.benny/pageindex/`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Open questions (must be resolved before the owning phase merges)\n\n- **OQ-1** (Phase 1) — Tree-builder model + per-node token budget under offline\n  mode (local reasoning model vs. cloud).\n- **OQ-2** (Phase 2) — `Section` schema reconciliation with existing\n  `Concept`/`Document` nodes and the `CORRELATES_WITH` enrichment overlay.\n- **OQ-3** (Phase 3) — Cross-doc candidate-link mechanism on summaries:\n  reasoning call vs. cheap clustering, and the threshold.\n- **OQ-4** (Phase 1) — Trigger: auto-detect structured docs vs. explicit\n  `strategy: \"vectorless\"` ingest flag.\n","numLines":113,"startLine":1,"totalLines":113}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4303ecde-0d43-4e57-98d2-a1149528cd27","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime\\docs\\requirements","sessionId":"8a533f4f-52c1-4883-9f06-3b7e51d615ce","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
