structured` retrieval route** — `retrieve_structured` node wired into `build_adaptive_rag_graph`: single node-select call over `abstract_outline` + load leaves; router classifies tree-backed docs to it. | PIX-F14, PIX-NFR2, GATE-PIX-LAT. | 🟡 **CODE LANDED** — node + routing wired; live single-call latency test TODO. |\n18\t\n19\tPhases 1–4 each require resolving their owning open question (see\n20\t[requirement.md §6](requirement.md#6-open-questions-must-be-resolved-before-the-owning-phase-merges))\n21\tbefore merge.\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## The runnable test (Phase 0 gate)\n26\t\n27\t```bash\n28\tcd runtime\n29\tpython -m pytest tests/test_pageindex_spine.py -v\n30\t# expected: 9 passed\n31\t```\n32\t\n33\tThis proves the spine's load-bearing claims offline, no LLM or DB:\n34\t\n35\t- **completeness** — `flatten_leaves` covers all 13 fixture leaves (>10, so the\n36\t  legacy `chunks[:10]` cap would fail this row);\n37\t- **provenance** — `node_id` survives into the fan-out sections;\n38\t- **determinism** — repeated partition is byte-identical;\n39\t- **cheap abstract** — `abstract_outline` carries no body text;\n40\t- **connected graph** — `build_section_edges` leaves no orphan node;\n41\t- **unique keys** — `validate_tree` flags duplicate/missing `node_id`.\n42\t\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t## Validation spike (recommended first real-corpus run, Phase 1/2)\n46\t\n47\tUse the existing **`prime_silo_self`** workspace (4 markdown docs already on\n48\tdisk; its graph is currently empty, so any result is a visible win):\n49\t\n50\t1. Build a tree for `USER_GUIDE.md` via `call_model()` and persist it.\n51\t2. Render `abstract_outline` — eyeball the indexed table-of-contents.\n52\t3. Fan `parallel_extract_triples` over `tree_to_sections(tree)`.\n53\t4. Compare the resulting Section graph + triples against today's (empty) graph.\n54\t\n55\tNo change to live default ingestion until tree-build latency is proven on the\n56\ttarget NPU hardware.\n57\t\n58\t---\n59\t\n60\t## Risk