{"parentUuid":"610394f2-b28c-4be8-ad79-8a472ce26f76","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RDN3tSMPMjXdeFCZh22Ui3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## OQ-1 spike — done, and it passed cleanly\n\nI sent `qwen3vl-it-4b-FLM` (already loaded on your Lemonade server) a generated PNG with an **unguessable** band order and asked it to read the colours left-to-right:\n\n```\n[response] 'blue, red, yellow'\n[verdict] all-colours=True  correct-order=True\n*** OQ-1 PASS: accepts image_url ('object') and sees the image. ***\n```\n\n**What this settles:**\n- **FLM does vision.** It accepts the standard OpenAI `image_url` **object** form (`image_url: {url: <data-uri>}`) over `127.0.0.1:13305/api/v1/chat/completions`.\n- **It genuinely sees** — the colour order was unpredictable, so a hallucinated \"red green blue\" would have failed. It got blue/red/yellow exactly.\n- **Lemonade/FLM is the primary VLM.** No lmstudio fallback needed (lmstudio/ollama were down anyway), and the `vlm_fallback` switch in the manifest stays as insurance only.\n\n**What I left behind:**\n- [`scripts/vision_spike.py`](runtime/scripts/vision_spike.py) — reproducible, zero-dependency (PNG built with stdlib zlib so it runs in any env). Re-run with `python scripts/vision_spike.py`, or point it at another endpoint via `--base/--model`.\n- OQ-1 marked **RESOLVED ✅** across [requirement.md](runtime/docs/requirements/13/requirement.md), [project_plan.md](runtime/docs/requirements/13/project_plan.md), and [acceptance_matrix.md](runtime/docs/requirements/13/acceptance_matrix.md), plus memory.\n\n## What the result tells us about Phase 1\n\nThe wiring is now well-scoped. The exact format that works is the OpenAI object form, so the change in [`call_model`](runtime/benny/core/models.py) is: let `messages[].content` be a **list** of parts and pass it through — but the load-bearing edit is the **local-executor short-circuit (models.py §5)**, which currently does `user_msg = msg.get(\"content\", \"\")` and would silently flatten/drop the image. That branch is where local models like FLM actually run, so it has to learn to forward list-form content (or hand a multimodal payload straight to the lemonade executor).\n\nTwo clean ways forward — your call:\n\n- **Phase 1 (multimodal router):** wire the list-form `content` through `call_model` + the lemonade executor, add the `qwen3vl` registry entry + `vision` role, and prove the round-trip *through Benny's own stack* (not just raw HTTP like the spike did). This unblocks the `describe_visuals` wave.\n- **Phase 0 (DocModel, no VLM):** the Docling element-tree + table→JSON + crop persist work, which is independent of the router and de-risks the parsing side.\n\nI'd do **Phase 1 next** while the spike findings are fresh — it's the smaller, now-de-risked piece, and it turns the spike's raw-HTTP proof into a real Benny capability. Want me to start there?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":167029,"output_tokens":1063,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":630,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":1063,"cache_read_input_tokens":167029,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":630},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcVuTNc7jEjRxKyo8dhuG","type":"assistant","uuid":"596091bb-f5aa-49f0-a652-18d622955a7c","timestamp":"2026-06-28T15:36:51.287Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime","sessionId":"8a533f4f-52c1-4883-9f06-3b7e51d615ce","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
