ructural only rejects: no header / no edges / unbalanced subgraph / prose. Also strip invalid `#` comments (mermaid uses `%%`).\n- Installed `@mermaid-js/mermaid-cli` in `packaging/` (pulls puppeteer+chromium); render-validate shells `node <cli.js>`; finds it via `BENNY_MMDC_CLI` env or packaging probe. NOT shipped in runtime bundle — dev/build-time quality gate only.\n- Eval results: **ADM cycle Fig 3-1 → valid Mermaid, 9/10**, all phases A-H + RM hub captured. Dense nested diagram Fig 3-2 → 4-6/10 (honest limit; graceful caption fallback). qwen3vl-4b is genuinely good on clean diagrams.\n\n**Phase 3 DONE ✅** (orchestrator+API): `benny/core/vision_pipeline.py` `enrich_docmodel()` runs ladder over all visuals, reuses Phase-0 table JSON, stitches enriched markdown + JSON sidecar IN READING ORDER with `<!-- docmodel id/page -->` provenance + figure_score; `write_enriched()` persists + drops enriched .md into data_in for rag_ingest→PageIndex (Section anchoring downstream, unchanged). `benny/api/vision_routes.py` (`/api/vision/docmodel`, `/enrich`) wired into `server.py`. Tests: test_vision_describe 14/14, test_vision_pipeline 6/6, test_docmodel 12/12, test_multimodal_call_model 8/8.\n\n**Eval harness/scripts (scratchpad + runtime/scripts):** `scripts/docmodel_smoke.py`, `scripts/vision_spike.py`; TOGAF DocModel scratch at `%TEMP%/togaf_eval/home/workspaces/togaf_eval` (1123 elements, 22 crops, 7 tables from 124-pg TOGAF). Run vision code via bundled python: `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 PYTHONPATH=\"<runtime>;<bundle>/site\" <bundle>/python/python.exe`.\n\n**Remaining (VIS-F16 + polish):** type-tagged Chroma chunks for surrogates; run the enrich workflow end-to-end through `benny enrich` manifest; filter docling phantom 0x0 tables (p52). Full-TOGAF capstone enrichment run launched 2026-06-28.","originalFile":"---\nname: project_prime_silo_vision_ingestion\ndescription: Prime-Silo vision-augmented ingestion (ADR-003 / VIS-001) — VLM turns figures/diagrams/charts/tables into graph surrogates\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 8a533f4f-52c1-4883-9f06-3b7e51d615ce\n---\n\nPrime-Silo next ingestion upgrade: **vision-augmented parsing** so Docling no longer drops every figure/diagram/chart (today [`extraction.py`] flattens to markdown and discards pictures; tables become flat markdown).\n\n**Design locked 2026-06-28** (user inspired by StarTrail-org/PixelRAG; downloading `qwen3vl-it-4b-FLM`):\n- **Strategy A only** (vision-augmented *parsing* → enrich text → existing PageIndex+triple+Chroma pipeline). PixelRAG/ColPali = \"Strategy B\" vision-*native* page-image retrieval, deliberately DEFERRED (different index/retriever; DocModel is the substrate B would reuse).\n- **Escalation ladder:** Docling element tree → classify → table→JSON, formula→LaTeX, picture sub-classify → illustration→caption / diagram→Mermaid|PlantUML / chart→JSON+desc. Validate every surrogate (parse/schema); caption fallback on fail (NO hollow success — recurring lesson, see [[memo_ray_token_audit_validation]]). Stitch in reading order. Anchor to ADR-002 PageIndex `Section` (node_id+page+bbox+crop) — reuse, don't reinvent provenance.\n- **Biggest code surface / risk:** `call_model()` is text-only — `messages[].content` is a str everywhere, and the local-executor short-circuit (models.py §5) pulls user_msg as a string → would silently drop images. Multimodal path must thread BOTH the LiteLLM branch and the local-executor branch.\n- **VLM target:** Lemonade/FLM primary. **OQ-1 RESOLVED ✅ 2026-06-28** — `scripts/vision_spike.py` proved `qwen3vl-it-4b-FLM` on Lemonade (`127.0.0.1:13305/api/v1`) accepts the OpenAI `image_url` **object** form and genuinely sees images (read unguessable blue/red/yellow band order). No lmstudio fallback needed. Phase 1 router wiring: allow list-form multimodal `content` through `call_model` + the local-executor short-circuit (models.py §5 currently flattens user_msg to str → would drop images).\n- **Honest caveat:** VLM surrogates are NOT byte-reproducible → exempt from SR-3 replay gate; get \"validated+cached+model_id\" guarantee instead (content-hash cache makes a given workspace stable after first pass).\n\n**Deliverables written (not yet coded):**\n- `runtime/architecture/ADR-003-vision-augmented-ingestion.md` (runtime ADR sequence; note: app-level `prime-silo/architecture/` has a SEPARATE ADR-003 about credential binding — two sequences).\n- `runtime/docs/requirements/13/` = VIS-001 (README, requirement, project_plan, acceptance_matrix), mirroring ADR-002/req-12 PageIndex convention.\n\nPhases: 0 structured DocModel (no VLM) → 1 multimodal router → 2 classifier+describers+validation → 3 graph integration. Validation corpus = **c5_test** workspace (UML/architecture PDFs already staged). Builds directly on [[project_memoray_primesilo_merge]] and the [[prime_silo_rag_ingestion_fix]] / PageIndex (ADR-002) work.\n\n**Phase 1 DONE ✅ 2026-06-28** (multimodal router, 8/8 tests pass incl. live round-trip through `call_model`):\n- `benny/core/local_executor.py`: added `_as_text`/`_is_multimodal`; `BaseOpenAICompatibleExecutor.generate` accepts list-form `prompt` (passes content verbatim; flattens text only for token/usage).\n- `benny/core/models.py`: `qwen3vl` registry entry (lemonade/qwen3vl-it-4b-FLM, use_for vision); `/no_think` injection (§2b) + token-count (§5) now guard list content so images aren't dropped/crashed.\n- `benny/core/vision.py` (NEW): `to_data_uri()` + `vision_message()` build the FLM-confirmed `image_url` **object** form.\n- Tests: `tests/test_multimodal_call_model.py` (offline guards + skippable live). `scripts/vision_spike.py` reproduces OQ-1.\n- Runtime python env = `C:\\Python314` (has litellm/tiktoken/httpx/fastapi; NO docling/Pillow — those are in the bundled benny env). Run tests with `PYTHONPATH=<runtime>`.\n- Caveat: pre-existing whole-suite pytest collection bug (`NotImplementedError: Stub class`) on ~20 unrelated files under broad `-k`; tests pass in isolation / by explicit path.\n\n**Product-bundle docling gap FIXED + verified (2026-06-28):** docling was in `runtime/requirements.txt` but MISSING from `BUNDLE_RUNTIME_REQUIREMENTS` in `packaging/scripts/assemble-runtime-bundle.js` (the shipped `site/` source of truth) → shipped EXE silently used basic fitz extraction (lost tables/layout). Added `docling>=2.4.0`+`Pillow>=10.0.0` to the assembler list, `tests/runtime_bundle_assembler_test.mjs` guard, and `requirements.txt`. Verified on product Python (python-build-standalone **3.11.9** x64, NOT 3.14): clean install, **full bundle co-resolves with docling — zero conflicts** (pydantic 2.13.4, numpy 2.4.6, torch **2.12.1+cpu**), co-import of full heavy stack OK. Full `site/` = **2.5 GB** (net +~1.5 GB). ⚠️ **Offline caveat:** docling fetches layout/table model weights from HF on FIRST USE → still needs network on first parse; pre-bake weights into bundle OR gate docling behind fitz fallback (Phase 0 sub-task).\n\n**Runtime bundle BUILT + docling verified in-product (2026-06-28):** `node packaging/scripts/pack-runtime-bundle.js` → `dist/runtime-bundle/runtime-bundle-win32-x64.tar.gz` (**909 MB**, sha256 262ac869…); docling-2.107.0/ibm-models/torch-2.12.1+cpu/Pillow present in bundled `site/`; import via the BUNDLED python+site (exactly what ships) succeeds. So the docling structured-extraction path now actually runs in the shipped product (was fitz-fallback before).\n**Build-path gotcha (skill was stale, now fixed):** `npm run desktop:localtest` sets `PRIME_SILO_BUNDLE_RUNTIME=1` but that var is **read nowhere** since v1.2.9 — localtest builds the SHELL APP ONLY. The runtime bundle (python+site incl docling + neo4j + jre) is a SEPARATE artifact built by `packaging/scripts/pack-runtime-bundle.js` (calls assemble-runtime-bundle.js → buildRuntimeBundle), shipped as a fetched release asset. Corrected the build-types table in `.claude/skills/devops-pipeline/SKILL.md`.\n\n**Phase 0 DONE ✅ 2026-06-28** (structured DocModel