{"parentUuid":"a3c3867a-0430-4fd4-99b1-3ba357821eaa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XqSXtCCRJ25BM71c3VT3gU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found the controls and the catch. Here's the accurate picture for **v1.5.0**.\n\n## Yes, the toggles exist — in the Bridge Documents panel\n\nIn the Bridge, on the Documents ingestion row (near the Ingest button) there are two checkboxes:\n- **\"Docling Extraction\"** (`useDocling`, default **on**)\n- **\"Enable OCR\"** (`doOcr`, default **off**) — greyed out until Docling is checked\n\nThey feed the existing `/rag/ingest` call (`use_docling` + `do_ocr`).\n\n## But in v1.5.0 they effectively do nothing — by design\n\nThis is the consequence of the lean pivot we made: **v1.5.0 does not bundle Docling** (we removed it to keep the runtime small and fully offline — no torch, no first-run model download). So when the runtime tries to honor \"Docling Extraction = on\", it hits an `ImportError` and **silently falls back to basic PyMuPDF text extraction**. And **OCR can't run at all without Docling**.\n\nNet: with the shipped 1.5.0 bundle, checking those boxes gives you the *same* plain-text result as leaving them off — no error, but no Docling structure and no OCR.\n\n## If you actually need Docling + OCR\n\nInstall Docling into the runtime's Python (it's not in the bundle). Roughly:\n\n```\n# from your benny-home runtime dir (the bundled python)\n.../runtime-bundle/python/python.exe -m pip install \"docling>=2.4.0\"\n```\n\nHeads-up on the cost you'd be opting back into: **~1.5 GB of torch/transformers**, and Docling **downloads its layout/table model weights from Hugging Face on the first parse** (so the first document needs network — the offline regression we deliberately avoided). After that, the toggles work and OCR becomes available.\n\n## Two things worth knowing\n\n1. **These toggles drive the *old* RAG ingestion path** (PDF → markdown → triples). The **new vision pipeline** from this release (figures → Mermaid, tables → JSON, the qwen3vl + qwen3-9b multi-model DocModel) is **not wired into the Bridge UI yet** — it's only reachable via the `/api/vision/docmodel` + `/api/vision/enrich` API and the `vision_ingestion` manifest. So the Documents toggles are unrelated to the vision-augmented work.\n2. For most v1.5.0 use, **leave them as-is** (basic PyMuPDF text is what you'll get regardless). Only install Docling if you specifically need scanned-PDF OCR or high-fidelity table/layout structure and can accept the size + first-run network.\n\nWant me to (a) add a small UI hint so the toggle reflects \"Docling not installed\" instead of silently falling back, and/or (b) wire the new vision figure→diagram pipeline into the Bridge as a proper \"Vision ingest\" option?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1077,"cache_read_input_tokens":653118,"output_tokens":3270,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1077,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3270,"cache_read_input_tokens":653118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1077},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcWP8MRA49x29zSUjkV5g","type":"assistant","uuid":"6588a6dd-7891-423c-a09b-52a07dc25af3","timestamp":"2026-06-28T21:40:10.971Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"8a533f4f-52c1-4883-9f06-3b7e51d615ce","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
