{"parentUuid":"ccbddc68-d452-4238-be4d-87f62ed4f3f4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3060823f-7656-419d-b301-c2942bbaf731","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LVuPz3np3ASv6oVxUeDvEW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// ADR-001 Phase D — runtime client.\n2\t//\n3\t// Single browser-side fetch helper for talking to the Benny FastAPI runtime\n4\t// through the shell's /api/runtime/<path> proxy. All Prime-Silo widgets and\n5\t// agent-composed layouts go through here so:\n6\t//\n7\t//   • Agent-scope header injection has exactly one chokepoint.\n8\t//   • Tests can swap the underlying fetch by overriding window.fetch.\n9\t//   • Phase F (.aamp.view signing) gets a stable seam to verify before\n10\t//     pinned layouts replay against the runtime.\n11\t//\n12\t// Public API\n13\t//   runtimeFetch(path, init)        — request the runtime; auto-injects the\n14\t//                                     active agent scope when one is set via\n15\t//                                     withAgentScope() or createAgentRuntimeClient\n16\t//   fetchAsAgent(path, init, opts)  — explicit agent request; injects\n17\t//                                     X-Benny-Agent-Scope unconditionally\n18\t//   readRuntimeJson(response)       — parse the runtime's JSON body\n19\t//   listWidgets()                   — convenience wrapper around GET /widgets\n20\t//\n21\t// Phase D3 additions\n22\t//   saveView(workspace, filename, content, options?)  — POST a JSON layout\n23\t//                                                       into agent_sandbox/views\n24\t//   loadView(workspace, filename, options?)           — GET + parse a saved view\n25\t//   listViews(workspace, options?)                    — GET the saved-view names\n26\t//\n27\t//   Bound clients gain the same three methods with the agent scope baked in.\n28\t//\n29\t// Phase F additions\n30\t//   signView(view, options?)                — POST /views/sign; returns\n31\t//                                              {signature, canonical_payload}.\n32\t//                                              Human-only: AgentScopeMiddleware\n33\t//                                              rejects agent-scoped POSTs to\n34\t//                                              /api/views/* with 403, so a bound\n35\t//                                              agent client calling this\n36\t//                                              surfaces the security boundary\n37\t//                                              as a RuntimeError(status=403).\n38\t//   verifyView(view, signature, options?)   — POST /views/verify; returns the\n39\t//                                              boolean result of the runtime's\n40\t//                                              constant-time HMAC compare.\n41\t//\n42\t// Phase F2 additions\n43\t//   pinView(workspace, sourceFilename, opts) — POST /views/pin; promotes an\n44\t//                                              agent draft from\n45\t//                                              agent_sandbox/views/<src> to\n46\t//                                              the canonical workspace\n47\t//                                              views/<dst>. The runtime\n48\t//                                              re-reads, signs, embeds the\n49\t//                                              signature inline, and emits\n50\t//                                              VIEW_PINNED. Human-only by\n51\t//                                              middleware.\n52\t//\n53\t// Phase F2b additions\n54\t//   loadPinnedView(workspace, filename, opts) — GET /views/load/<ws>/<fname>;\n55\t//                                              reads a pinned view AND\n56\t//                                              verifies its embedded\n57\t//                                              signature in one round-trip.\n58\t//                                              Returns\n59\t//                                              {view, signature, valid, …}.\n60\t//                                              Reads are open to agents too\n61\t//                                              — pinned views are\n62\t//                                              deterministic-zone artefacts\n63\t//                                              and replay must succeed\n64\t//                                              under any caller. The\n65\t//                                              runtime is the sole holder\n66\t//                                              of BENNY_HMAC_KEY; the\n67\t//                                              browser only consumes\n68\t//                                              `valid`.\n69\t//\n70\t// Phase D2 additions\n71\t//   createAgentRuntimeClient(scope) — bound client whose every call auto-injects\n72\t//                                     the agent scope. Hand this to skills /\n73\t//                                     widgets via options.runtimeClient and the\n74\t//                                     X-Benny-Agent-Scope header is on every\n75\t//                                     /api/runtime/* hop, audited at the\n76\t//                                     AgentScopeMiddleware in Benny.\n77\t//   withAgentScope(scope, fn)       — run fn() with scope set as the active\n78\t//                                     agent scope; restores on return.\n79\t//                                     Synchronous code path inside fn() —\n80\t//                                     including the *first* awaited runtimeFetch —\n81\t//                                     picks up the scope. Awaiting through\n82\t//                                     other tasks loses context (no\n83\t//                                     AsyncLocalStorage in browsers); for\n84\t//                                     long-running agent loops use\n85\t//                                     createAgentRuntimeClient instead.\n86\t//   getActiveAgentScope()           — returns the currently active scope or null.\n87\t//\n88\t// Path semantics: callers pass paths *relative to the runtime API root*.\n89\t//   listWidgets()                  → /api/runtime/widgets\n90\t//   runtimeFetch(\"/agent_sandbox/health\") → /api/runtime/agent_sandbox/health\n91\t//\n92\t// Errors are thrown with .status set when the runtime returns non-2xx.\n93\t\n94\t// Two server-authoritative proxy facades (ADR-001 confused-deputy fix):\n95\t//   • RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX        — human path. The shell injects the trusted\n96\t//     Benny key and STRIPS any X-Benny-Agent-Scope, so a human request runs\n97\t//     under normal RBAC.\n98\t//   • AGENT_RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX  — agent path. The shell injects a distinct,\n99\t//     sandbox-bound key and forces scope server-side. Agent traffic MUST use\n100\t//     this path; the scope is no longer something the browser can assert.\n101\t// Routing is driven by the active agent context (_activeAgentScope): unscoped\n102\t// calls go to the human path, scoped calls (withAgentScope / bound client /\n103\t// fetchAsAgent) go to the agent path.\n104\tconst RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX = \"/api/runtime\";\n105\tconst AGENT_RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX = \"/api/agent-runtime\";\n106\t\n107\tconst VALID_AGENT_SCOPES = new Set([\"sandbox\", \"read_only\"]);\n108\t\n109\tconst AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER = \"X-Benny-Agent-Scope\";\n110\t\n111\t// Module-scoped active agent scope. withAgentScope() pushes/pops; bound\n112\t// clients read it via the call site. The unbound runtimeFetch auto-injects\n113\t// this onto outgoing requests when no header was set explicitly.\n114\tlet _activeAgentScope = null;\n115\t\n116\tfunction joinPath(prefix, path) {\n117\t  if (!path || path === \"/\") {\n118\t    return prefix;\n119\t  }\n120\t  return path.startsWith(\"/\") ? `${prefix}${path}` : `${prefix}/${path}`;\n121\t}\n122\t\n123\t// Pick the proxy facade for the current call. Any active agent scope (set via\n124\t// withAgentScope, fetchAsAgent, or a bound client) routes through the agent\n125\t// path, where the shell pins the scope server-side; everything else is human\n126\t// traffic on the trusted path.\n127\tfunction activeRuntimePrefix() {\n128\t  return _activeAgentScope ? AGENT_RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX : RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX;\n129\t}\n130\t\n131\tasync function readErrorDetail(response) {\n132\t  try {\n133\t    const body = await response.text();\n134\t    if (!body) {\n135\t      return null;\n136\t    }\n137\t    try {\n138\t      return JSON.parse(body);\n139\t    } catch {\n140\t      return { detail: body };\n141\t    }\n142\t  } catch {\n143\t    return null;\n144\t  }\n145\t}\n146\t\n147\tfunction createRuntimeError(response, body) {\n148\t  const detail =\n149\t    (body && (body.detail || body.error)) ||\n150\t    `Runtime ${response.status} ${response.statusText || \"\"}`.trim();\n151\t  const error = new Error(detail);\n152\t  error.name = \"RuntimeError\";\n153\t  error.status = response.status;\n154\t  error.body = body;\n155\t  return error;\n156\t}\n157\t\n158\tfunction validateScope(scope) {\n159\t  if (!VALID_AGENT_SCOPES.has(scope)) {\n160\t    throw new Error(\n161\t      `Invalid agent scope: ${scope}. Expected one of ${[...VALID_AGENT_SCOPES].join(\", \")}.`\n162\t    );\n163\t  }\n164\t}\n165\t\n166\t/**\n167\t * Make a request to the Benny runtime through the shell proxy.\n168\t *\n169\t * Without an active agent scope this is a *human-driven* request and the\n170\t * runtime gates it via regular RBAC. When called from inside a\n171\t * `withAgentScope()` block — or via a client returned from\n172\t * `createAgentRuntimeClient(scope)` — the active scope is auto-injected as\n173\t * the `X-Benny-Agent-Scope` header so the runtime's `AgentScopeMiddleware`\n174\t * enforces the ADR-001 boundary on this hop.\n175\t *\n176\t * If the caller already set the header on `init.headers`, it wins — explicit\n177\t * intent beats ambient context.\n178\t */\n179\texport async function runtimeFetch(path, init = {}) {\n180\t  const url = joinPath(activeRuntimePrefix(), path);\n181\t  const headers = new Headers(init.headers || {});\n182\t\n183\t  // The scope header is belt-and-suspenders: the agent-path proxy strips and\n184\t  // re-asserts it server-side. We still send it so audit logs and a\n185\t  // not-yet-upgraded proxy both see the intended scope.\n186\t  if (_activeAgentScope && !headers.has(AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER)) {\n187\t    headers.set(AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER, _activeAgentScope);\n188\t  }\n189\t\n190\t  const response = await fetch(url, {\n191\t    ...init,\n192\t    headers,\n193\t    credentials: init.credentials || \"same-origin\"\n194\t  });\n195\t\n196\t  if (!response.ok) {\n197\t    const body = await readErrorDetail(response);\n198\t    throw createRuntimeError(response, body);\n199\t  }\n200\t\n201\t  return response;\n202\t}\n203\t\n204\t/**\n205\t * Same as runtimeFetch, but injects the X-Benny-Agent-Scope header\n206\t * unconditionally. Default scope is \"sandbox\" (writes confined to\n207\t * agent_sandbox/). Pass {scope:\"read_only\"} to disallow writes entirely.\n208\t *\n209\t * Agent-authored writes that target anything outside /api/runtime/agent_sandbox/\n210\t * will be rejected by the runtime with HTTP 403.\n211\t */\n212\texport async function fetchAsAgent(path, init = {}, options = {}) {\n213\t  const scope = options.scope || \"sandbox\";\n214\t  validateScope(scope);\n215\t\n216\t  const headers = new Headers(init.headers || {});\n217\t  headers.set(AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER, scope);\n218\t\n219\t  // Run inside the agent scope context so runtimeFetch routes to the\n220\t  // agent-runtime facade (and not the trusted human path) for this call.\n221\t  return withAgentScope(scope, () => runtimeFetch(path, { ...init, headers }));\n222\t}\n223\t\n224\texport async function readRuntimeJson(response) {\n225\t  const text = await response.text();\n226\t  return text ? JSON.parse(text) : null;\n227\t}\n228\t\n229\t/**\n230\t * Convenience: GET /api/runtime/widgets and parse the JSON body. Throws\n231\t * RuntimeError if the runtime is unreachable or returns non-2xx.\n232\t *\n233\t * When called from an agent context (withAgentScope or\n234\t * createAgentRuntimeClient), the listing fetch is itself tagged with the\n235\t * agent scope header so the audit log records who asked.\n236\t */\n237\texport async function listWidgets() {\n238\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/widgets\");\n239\t  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n240\t}\n241\t\n242\t/**\n243\t * Phase D3 — save a JSON layout view into the workspace's\n244\t * `agent_sandbox/views/` subtree.\n245\t *\n246\t * The runtime endpoint validates that the body parses as JSON and forces\n247\t * `subdir=\"views\"` so a stray call cannot silently land in `drafts/` or\n248\t * `notes/`. Callers may pass either a JSON string or any JSON-serialisable\n249\t * object — objects are stringified before send so the JSON validation on\n250\t * both sides agrees.\n251\t *\n252\t * Filename convention: `<id>.aamp.view`, but enforcement happens server-side\n253\t * (no path separators, no leading dot). This helper does not invent the\n254\t * extension — Phase F .aamp.view signing belongs at the manifest layer, not\n255\t * here.\n256\t *\n257\t * Returns the runtime's `SandboxWriteResponse`:\n258\t *   { status: \"written\", workspace, relative_path, bytes_written }\n259\t *\n260\t * Auto-injects the active agent scope when one is set; the bound-client\n261\t * variant forces it. Without scope this is a human-driven write — the runtime\n262\t * still validates JSON and path containment.\n263\t *\n264\t * @param {string} workspace\n265\t * @param {string} filename\n266\t * @param {string | object} content\n267\t * @param {{ agentId?: string }} [options]\n268\t * @returns {Promise<{status: \"written\", workspace: string, relative_path: string, bytes_written: number}>}\n269\t */\n270\texport async function saveView(workspace, filename, content, options = {}) {\n271\t  const body = serialiseViewContent(content);\n272\t  const payload = {\n273\t    workspace,\n274\t    subdir: \"views\",\n275\t    filename,\n276\t    content: body,\n277\t    agent_id: options.agentId || \"anonymous_agent\"\n278\t  };\n279\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/agent_sandbox/views/save\", {\n280\t    method: \"POST\",\n281\t    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n282\t    body: JSON.stringify(payload)\n283\t  });\n284\t  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n285\t}\n286\t\n287\t/**\n288\t * Phase D3 — load a saved view from `agent_sandbox/views/`.\n289\t *\n290\t * Returns the runtime's read envelope:\n291\t *   { workspace, subdir: \"views\", filename, relative_path, content, bytes }\n292\t *\n293\t * `content` is the raw UTF-8 string the file contains. By default the helper\n294\t * also parses it as JSON and exposes the result on the `view` property —\n295\t * pass `{ parseJson: false }` to skip parsing for non-JSON layouts (none\n296\t * exist today; the runtime guards JSON on save, but the read endpoint is\n297\t * format-agnostic).\n298\t *\n299\t * @param {string} workspace\n300\t * @param {string} filename\n301\t * @param {{ parseJson?: boolean }} [options]\n302\t */\n303\texport async function loadView(workspace, filename, options = {}) {\n304\t  const path = `/agent_sandbox/read/${encodeURIComponent(workspace)}/views/${encodeURIComponent(filename)}`;\n305\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(path);\n306\t  const envelope = await readRuntimeJson(response);\n307\t  const parseJson = options.parseJson !== false;\n308\t  if (parseJson && envelope && typeof envelope.content === \"string\") {\n309\t    try {\n310\t      envelope.view = JSON.parse(envelope.content);\n311\t    } catch (err) {\n312\t      const error = new Error(`loadView: stored content is not valid JSON: ${err.message}`);\n313\t      error.name = \"RuntimeError\";\n314\t      error.cause = err;\n315\t      throw error;\n316\t    }\n317\t  }\n318\t  return envelope;\n319\t}\n320\t\n321\t/**\n322\t * Phase D3 — list saved view filenames for a workspace.\n323\t *\n324\t * Returns the entries array directly (the runtime envelope's `entries` field).\n325\t * Pass `{ raw: true }` to get the full envelope `{ workspace, subdir, entries }`\n326\t * instead.\n327\t *\n328\t * @param {string} workspace\n329\t * @param {{ raw?: boolean }} [options]\n330\t */\n331\texport async function listViews(workspace, options = {}) {\n332\t  const path = `/agent_sandbox/list/${encodeURIComponent(workspace)}/views`;\n333\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(path);\n334\t  const envelope = await readRuntimeJson(response);\n335\t  if (options.raw) {\n336\t    return envelope;\n337\t  }\n338\t  return envelope && Array.isArray(envelope.entries) ? envelope.entries : [];\n339\t}\n340\t\n341\t/**\n342\t * Phase F — sign a `.aamp.view` layout via the runtime's HMAC chokepoint.\n343\t *\n344\t * Posts the view to `/api/views/sign` (intentionally outside the agent_sandbox\n345\t * prefix). `AgentScopeMiddleware` blocks any agent-scoped POST here with HTTP\n346\t * 403, so calling `signView` from a bound agent client surfaces the security\n347\t * boundary as a `RuntimeError(status=403)` — the runtime is the enforcer, not\n348\t * this module.\n349\t *\n350\t * Accepts a JSON-serialisable view object. The runtime computes HMAC-SHA256\n351\t * over a canonical payload (sorted keys, no whitespace, `signature` field\n352\t * stripped) and returns:\n353\t *\n354\t *   { signature: { algorithm, value, signed_at }, canonical_payload: \"...\" }\n355\t *\n356\t * The canonical payload is returned so callers can audit exactly what was\n357\t * signed before embedding the signature back into the view.\n358\t *\n359\t * @param {object} view\n360\t * @param {{ }} [options]\n361\t * @returns {Promise<{signature: {algorithm: string, value: string, signed_at: string}, canonical_payload: string}>}\n362\t */\n363\texport async function signView(view, options = {}) {\n364\t  if (!view || typeof view !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(view)) {\n365\t    throw new Error(\"signView: view must be a JSON object.\");\n366\t  }\n367\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/views/sign\", {\n368\t    method: \"POST\",\n369\t    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n370\t    body: JSON.stringify({ view })\n371\t  });\n372\t  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n373\t}\n374\t\n375\t/**\n376\t * Phase F — verify an HMAC-SHA256 signature over a `.aamp.view` payload.\n377\t *\n378\t * Posts `{view, signature}` to `/api/views/verify` and returns the runtime's\n379\t * boolean result. The runtime uses `hmac.compare_digest` to avoid timing\n380\t * leaks; clients must treat any non-true result as a verification failure.\n381\t *\n382\t * Like `signView`, this endpoint sits outside `/api/agent_sandbox/`, so a\n383\t * bound agent client invoking it triggers the middleware's 403 — verification\n384\t * is a human / shell-server action.\n385\t *\n386\t * @param {object} view\n387\t * @param {{algorithm: string, value: string, signed_at: string}} signature\n388\t * @param {{ }} [options]\n389\t * @returns {Promise<boolean>}\n390\t */\n391\texport async function verifyView(view, signature, options = {}) {\n392\t  if (!view || typeof view !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(view)) {\n393\t    throw new Error(\"verifyView: view must be a JSON object.\");\n394\t  }\n395\t  if (!signature || typeof signature !== \"object\") {\n396\t    throw new Error(\"verifyView: signature must be an envelope object.\");\n397\t  }\n398\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/views/verify\", {\n399\t    method: \"POST\",\n400\t    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n401\t    body: JSON.stringify({ view, signature })\n402\t  });\n403\t  const body = await readRuntimeJson(response);\n404\t  return Boolean(body && body.valid);\n405\t}\n406\t\n407\t/**\n408\t * Phase F2 — promote an agent-drafted view to a signed, canonical workspace\n409\t * location.\n410\t *\n411\t * Posts `{workspace, source_filename, target_filename?, pinned_by?}` to\n412\t * `/api/views/pin`. The runtime re-reads the draft from\n413\t * `agent_sandbox/views/<source_filename>`, signs it, embeds the signature\n414\t * inline, writes to `<workspace>/views/<target_filename>` (defaulting to\n415\t * `source_filename`), and emits a `VIEW_PINNED` audit event.\n416\t *\n417\t * Same human-only boundary as `signView` — `/api/views/pin` lives outside\n418\t * `/api/agent_sandbox/`, so a bound agent client invoking this triggers\n419\t * `RuntimeError(status=403)`.\n420\t *\n421\t * Returns the runtime's `PinViewResponse`:\n422\t *   {\n423\t *     workspace, source_relative_path, pinned_relative_path,\n424\t *     bytes_written, signature: { algorithm, value, signed_at }\n425\t *   }\n426\t *\n427\t * @param {string} workspace\n428\t * @param {string} sourceFilename — must match `agent_sandbox/views/<filename>`\n429\t * @param {{ targetFilename?: string, pinnedBy?: string }} [options]\n430\t */\n431\texport async function pinView(workspace, sourceFilename, options = {}) {\n432\t  if (typeof workspace !== \"string\" || !workspace) {\n433\t    throw new Error(\"pinView: workspace is required.\");\n434\t  }\n435\t  if (typeof sourceFilename !== \"string\" || !sourceFilename) {\n436\t    throw new Error(\"pinView: sourceFilename is required.\");\n437\t  }\n438\t  const payload = {\n439\t    workspace,\n440\t    source_filename: sourceFilename\n441\t  };\n442\t  if (options.targetFilename) {\n443\t    payload.target_filename = options.targetFilename;\n444\t  }\n445\t  if (options.pinnedBy) {\n446\t    payload.pinned_by = options.pinnedBy;\n447\t  }\n448\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/views/pin\", {\n449\t    method: \"POST\",\n450\t    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n451\t    body: JSON.stringify(payload)\n452\t  });\n453\t  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n454\t}\n455\t\n456\t/**\n457\t * Phase F2b — read a pinned view AND verify its embedded signature in one\n458\t * round-trip.\n459\t *\n460\t * GETs ``/api/views/load/<workspace>/<filename>``. The runtime reads\n461\t * ``$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/<ws>/views/<filename>``, extracts the\n462\t * ``signature`` field embedded by ``pinView``, recomputes the HMAC against\n463\t * the rest of the canonical payload, and returns:\n464\t *\n465\t *   {\n466\t *     workspace, filename, relative_path, bytes,\n467\t *     view: { …, signature: {algorithm, value, signed_at} },\n468\t *     signature: { algorithm, value, signed_at } | null,\n469\t *     valid: boolean\n470\t *   }\n471\t *\n472\t * ``valid: false`` is NOT an HTTP error — the caller is expected to branch\n473\t * on it. A missing or malformed inline signature surfaces as ``valid: false``\n474\t * with ``signature: null``; structural problems (no such file, body is not\n475\t * JSON, body is not an object) surface as HTTP 404 / 400.\n476\t *\n477\t * Reads are unrestricted by ``AgentScopeMiddleware`` so this works from any\n478\t * caller — human, bound agent client, or anonymous shell. The runtime is\n479\t * the only holder of ``BENNY_HMAC_KEY``; the browser never re-signs and\n480\t * never trusts a client-side check.\n481\t *\n482\t * @param {string} workspace\n483\t * @param {string} filename\n484\t * @param {{ }} [options]\n485\t * @returns {Promise<{\n486\t *   workspace: string,\n487\t *   filename: string,\n488\t *   relative_path: string,\n489\t *   bytes: number,\n490\t *   view: object,\n491\t *   signature: {algorithm: string, value: string, signed_at: string} | null,\n492\t *   valid: boolean\n493\t * }>}\n494\t */\n495\texport async function loadPinnedView(workspace, filename, options = {}) {\n496\t  if (typeof workspace !== \"string\" || !workspace) {\n497\t    throw new Error(\"loadPinnedView: workspace is required.\");\n498\t  }\n499\t  if (typeof filename !== \"string\" || !filename) {\n500\t    throw new Error(\"loadPinnedView: filename is required.\");\n501\t  }\n502\t  const path = `/views/load/${encodeURIComponent(workspace)}/${encodeURIComponent(filename)}`;\n503\t  const response = await runtimeFetch(path);\n504\t  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n505\t}\n506\t\n507\tfunction serialiseViewContent(content) {\n508\t  if (typeof content === \"string\") {\n509\t    return content;\n510\t  }\n511\t  if (content === null || content === undefined) {\n512\t    throw new Error(\"saveView: content must be a JSON string or a JSON-serialisable object.\");\n513\t  }\n514\t  return JSON.stringify(content);\n515\t}\n516\t\n517\t/**\n518\t * Phase D2 — synchronous agent-scope context.\n519\t *\n520\t * Sets the active agent scope for the duration of `fn()` and restores the\n521\t * previous scope on return. Browsers don't have AsyncLocalStorage, so the\n522\t * scope only auto-applies for the synchronous code path inside `fn` —\n523\t * including the *first* await on `runtimeFetch`. Once `fn` resolves, the\n524\t * scope is gone. For long-running agent loops, use\n525\t * `createAgentRuntimeClient(scope)` and pass the bound client through.\n526\t *\n527\t * Nesting works: inner scopes shadow outer scopes and the outer scope is\n528\t * restored when the inner block returns.\n529\t *\n530\t * @param {\"sandbox\"|\"read_only\"} scope\n531\t * @param {() => T | Promise<T>} fn\n532\t * @returns {T | Promise<T>}\n533\t */\n534\texport function withAgentScope(scope, fn) {\n535\t  validateScope(scope);\n536\t  if (typeof fn !== \"function\") {\n537\t    throw new Error(\"withAgentScope: fn must be a function.\");\n538\t  }\n539\t  const previous = _activeAgentScope;\n540\t  _activeAgentScope = scope;\n541\t  try {\n542\t    const result = fn();\n543\t    if (result && typeof result.then === \"function\") {\n544\t      return result.finally(() => {\n545\t        _activeAgentScope = previous;\n546\t      });\n547\t    }\n548\t    _activeAgentScope = previous;\n549\t    return result;\n550\t  } catch (err) {\n551\t    _activeAgentScope = previous;\n552\t    throw err;\n553\t  }\n554\t}\n555\t\n556\t/**\n557\t * Phase D2 — return the active agent scope, or null when no scope is in\n558\t * effect. Useful for assertions and structured logging.\n559\t */\n560\texport function getActiveAgentScope() {\n561\t  return _activeAgentScope;\n562\t}\n563\t\n564\t/**\n565\t * Phase D2 — bound runtime client whose every call auto-injects the given\n566\t * agent scope. The space-agent browser-resident agent runtime should call\n567\t * `createAgentRuntimeClient(\"sandbox\")` once per turn and pass the result as\n568\t * `options.runtimeClient` to whatever skill / widget / tool it spawns. Each\n569\t * outgoing /api/runtime/* hop carries `X-Benny-Agent-Scope`, so the runtime's\n570\t * `AgentScopeMiddleware` audits the call regardless of which code path\n571\t * originates it.\n572\t *\n573\t * The bound client is shape-compatible with what widgets already accept via\n574\t * `options.runtimeClient` ({ runtimeFetch, readRuntimeJson, … }) — no widget\n575\t * changes required.\n576\t *\n577\t * @param {\"sandbox\"|\"read_only\"} scope\n578\t * @returns {{\n579\t *   scope: string,\n580\t *   runtimeFetch: (path: string, init?: object) => Promise<Response>,\n581\t *   fetchAsAgent: (path: string, init?: object, options?: {scope?: string}) => Promise<Response>,\n582\t *   readRuntimeJson: (response: Response) => Promise<unknown>,\n583\t *   listWidgets: () => Promise<unknown>,\n584\t *   saveView: (workspace: string, filename: string, content: string | object, options?: {agentId?: string}) => Promise<unknown>,\n585\t *   loadView: (workspace: string, filename: string, options?: {parseJson?: boolean}) => Promise<unknown>,\n586\t *   listViews: (workspace: string, options?: {raw?: boolean}) => Promise<unknown>,\n587\t *   signView: (view: object, options?: object) => Promise<unknown>,\n588\t *   verifyView: (view: object, signature: object, options?: object) => Promise<boolean>,\n589\t *   pinView: (workspace: string, sourceFilename: string, options?: {targetFilename?: string, pinnedBy?: string}) => Promise<unknown>,\n590\t *   loadPinnedView: (workspace: string, filename: string, options?: object) => Promise<unknown>\n591\t * }}\n592\t */\n593\texport function createAgentRuntimeClient(scope) {\n594\t  validateScope(scope);\n595\t  return {\n596\t    get scope() {\n597\t      return scope;\n598\t    },\n599\t    runtimeFetch(path, init = {}) {\n600\t      return fetchAsAgent(path, init, { scope });\n601\t    },\n602\t    fetchAsAgent(path, init = {}, options = {}) {\n603\t      return fetchAsAgent(path, init, { scope: options.scope || scope });\n604\t    },\n605\t    readRuntimeJson(response) {\n606\t      return readRuntimeJson(response);\n607\t    },\n608\t    async listWidgets() {\n609\t      const response = await fetchAsAgent(\"/widgets\", {}, { scope });\n610\t      return readRuntimeJson(response);\n611\t    },\n612\t    saveView(workspace, filename, content, options = {}) {\n613\t      return withAgentScope(scope, () => saveView(workspace, filename, content, options));\n614\t    },\n615\t    loadView(workspace, filename, options = {}) {\n616\t      return withAgentScope(scope, () => loadView(workspace, filename, options));\n617\t    },\n618\t    listViews(workspace, options = {}) {\n619\t      return withAgentScope(scope, () => listViews(workspace, options));\n620\t    },\n621\t    // Phase F — the bound client tags signView/verifyView with the agent\n622\t    // scope, but the routes live outside /api/agent_sandbox/ so the runtime\n623\t    // middleware will 403 every agent-scoped POST. The 403 is the boundary;\n624\t    // do not silently downgrade by stripping the header here.\n625\t    signView(view, options = {}) {\n626\t      return withAgentScope(scope, () => signView(view, options));\n627\t    },\n628\t    verifyView(view, signature, options = {}) {\n629\t      return withAgentScope(scope, () => verifyView(view, signature, options));\n630\t    },\n631\t    // Phase F2 — same defence-in-depth: pinView from a bound agent client\n632\t    // forwards the scope header and the runtime's middleware issues 403.\n633\t    // Pinning is human-only by middleware policy.\n634\t    pinView(workspace, sourceFilename, options = {}) {\n635\t      return withAgentScope(scope, () => pinView(workspace, sourceFilename, options));\n636\t    },\n637\t    // Phase F2b — reads are unrestricted by AgentScopeMiddleware, so this\n638\t    // call succeeds for agents too. We still forward the scope header so\n639\t    // the runtime audit log records which actor read the pinned artefact.\n640\t    loadPinnedView(workspace, filename, options = {}) {\n641\t      return withAgentScope(scope, () => loadPinnedView(workspace, filename, options));\n642\t    }\n643\t  };\n644\t}\n645\t\n646\texport const __testing = {\n647\t  RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX,\n648\t  AGENT_RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX,\n649\t  AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER,\n650\t  activeRuntimePrefix,\n651\t  joinPath,\n652\t  resetAgentScope() {\n653\t    _activeAgentScope = null;\n654\t  },\n655\t  getActiveAgentScopeForTest() {\n656\t    return _activeAgentScope;\n657\t  }\n658\t};\n659\t"}]},"uuid":"10ad8ef4-8e0a-4c41-ad1a-b34d8368600b","timestamp":"2026-06-29T07:59:20.748Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\app\\L0\\_all\\mod\\_prime_silo\\runtime_client\\runtime-client.js","content":"// ADR-001 Phase D — runtime client.\n//\n// Single browser-side fetch helper for talking to the Benny FastAPI runtime\n// through the shell's /api/runtime/<path> proxy. All Prime-Silo widgets and\n// agent-composed layouts go through here so:\n//\n//   • Agent-scope header injection has exactly one chokepoint.\n//   • Tests can swap the underlying fetch by overriding window.fetch.\n//   • Phase F (.aamp.view signing) gets a stable seam to verify before\n//     pinned layouts replay against the runtime.\n//\n// Public API\n//   runtimeFetch(path, init)        — request the runtime; auto-injects the\n//                                     active agent scope when one is set via\n//                                     withAgentScope() or createAgentRuntimeClient\n//   fetchAsAgent(path, init, opts)  — explicit agent request; injects\n//                                     X-Benny-Agent-Scope unconditionally\n//   readRuntimeJson(response)       — parse the runtime's JSON body\n//   listWidgets()                   — convenience wrapper around GET /widgets\n//\n// Phase D3 additions\n//   saveView(workspace, filename, content, options?)  — POST a JSON layout\n//                                                       into agent_sandbox/views\n//   loadView(workspace, filename, options?)           — GET + parse a saved view\n//   listViews(workspace, options?)                    — GET the saved-view names\n//\n//   Bound clients gain the same three methods with the agent scope baked in.\n//\n// Phase F additions\n//   signView(view, options?)                — POST /views/sign; returns\n//                                              {signature, canonical_payload}.\n//                                              Human-only: AgentScopeMiddleware\n//                                              rejects agent-scoped POSTs to\n//                                              /api/views/* with 403, so a bound\n//                                              agent client calling this\n//                                              surfaces the security boundary\n//                                              as a RuntimeError(status=403).\n//   verifyView(view, signature, options?)   — POST /views/verify; returns the\n//                                              boolean result of the runtime's\n//                                              constant-time HMAC compare.\n//\n// Phase F2 additions\n//   pinView(workspace, sourceFilename, opts) — POST /views/pin; promotes an\n//                                              agent draft from\n//                                              agent_sandbox/views/<src> to\n//                                              the canonical workspace\n//                                              views/<dst>. The runtime\n//                                              re-reads, signs, embeds the\n//                                              signature inline, and emits\n//                                              VIEW_PINNED. Human-only by\n//                                              middleware.\n//\n// Phase F2b additions\n//   loadPinnedView(workspace, filename, opts) — GET /views/load/<ws>/<fname>;\n//                                              reads a pinned view AND\n//                                              verifies its embedded\n//                                              signature in one round-trip.\n//                                              Returns\n//                                              {view, signature, valid, …}.\n//                                              Reads are open to agents too\n//                                              — pinned views are\n//                                              deterministic-zone artefacts\n//                                              and replay must succeed\n//                                              under any caller. The\n//                                              runtime is the sole holder\n//                                              of BENNY_HMAC_KEY; the\n//                                              browser only consumes\n//                                              `valid`.\n//\n// Phase D2 additions\n//   createAgentRuntimeClient(scope) — bound client whose every call auto-injects\n//                                     the agent scope. Hand this to skills /\n//                                     widgets via options.runtimeClient and the\n//                                     X-Benny-Agent-Scope header is on every\n//                                     /api/runtime/* hop, audited at the\n//                                     AgentScopeMiddleware in Benny.\n//   withAgentScope(scope, fn)       — run fn() with scope set as the active\n//                                     agent scope; restores on return.\n//                                     Synchronous code path inside fn() —\n//                                     including the *first* awaited runtimeFetch —\n//                                     picks up the scope. Awaiting through\n//                                     other tasks loses context (no\n//                                     AsyncLocalStorage in browsers); for\n//                                     long-running agent loops use\n//                                     createAgentRuntimeClient instead.\n//   getActiveAgentScope()           — returns the currently active scope or null.\n//\n// Path semantics: callers pass paths *relative to the runtime API root*.\n//   listWidgets()                  → /api/runtime/widgets\n//   runtimeFetch(\"/agent_sandbox/health\") → /api/runtime/agent_sandbox/health\n//\n// Errors are thrown with .status set when the runtime returns non-2xx.\n\n// Two server-authoritative proxy facades (ADR-001 confused-deputy fix):\n//   • RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX        — human path. The shell injects the trusted\n//     Benny key and STRIPS any X-Benny-Agent-Scope, so a human request runs\n//     under normal RBAC.\n//   • AGENT_RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX  — agent path. The shell injects a distinct,\n//     sandbox-bound key and forces scope server-side. Agent traffic MUST use\n//     this path; the scope is no longer something the browser can assert.\n// Routing is driven by the active agent context (_activeAgentScope): unscoped\n// calls go to the human path, scoped calls (withAgentScope / bound client /\n// fetchAsAgent) go to the agent path.\nconst RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX = \"/api/runtime\";\nconst AGENT_RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX = \"/api/agent-runtime\";\n\nconst VALID_AGENT_SCOPES = new Set([\"sandbox\", \"read_only\"]);\n\nconst AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER = \"X-Benny-Agent-Scope\";\n\n// Module-scoped active agent scope. withAgentScope() pushes/pops; bound\n// clients read it via the call site. The unbound runtimeFetch auto-injects\n// this onto outgoing requests when no header was set explicitly.\nlet _activeAgentScope = null;\n\nfunction joinPath(prefix, path) {\n  if (!path || path === \"/\") {\n    return prefix;\n  }\n  return path.startsWith(\"/\") ? `${prefix}${path}` : `${prefix}/${path}`;\n}\n\n// Pick the proxy facade for the current call. Any active agent scope (set via\n// withAgentScope, fetchAsAgent, or a bound client) routes through the agent\n// path, where the shell pins the scope server-side; everything else is human\n// traffic on the trusted path.\nfunction activeRuntimePrefix() {\n  return _activeAgentScope ? AGENT_RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX : RUNTIME_PROXY_PREFIX;\n}\n\nasync function readErrorDetail(response) {\n  try {\n    const body = await response.text();\n    if (!body) {\n      return null;\n    }\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(body);\n    } catch {\n      return { detail: body };\n    }\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction createRuntimeError(response, body) {\n  const detail =\n    (body && (body.detail || body.error)) ||\n    `Runtime ${response.status} ${response.statusText || \"\"}`.trim();\n  const error = new Error(detail);\n  error.name = \"RuntimeError\";\n  error.status = response.status;\n  error.body = body;\n  return error;\n}\n\nfunction validateScope(scope) {\n  if (!VALID_AGENT_SCOPES.has(scope)) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `Invalid agent scope: ${scope}. Expected one of ${[...VALID_AGENT_SCOPES].join(\", \")}.`\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Make a request to the Benny runtime through the shell proxy.\n *\n * Without an active agent scope this is a *human-driven* request and the\n * runtime gates it via regular RBAC. When called from inside a\n * `withAgentScope()` block — or via a client returned from\n * `createAgentRuntimeClient(scope)` — the active scope is auto-injected as\n * the `X-Benny-Agent-Scope` header so the runtime's `AgentScopeMiddleware`\n * enforces the ADR-001 boundary on this hop.\n *\n * If the caller already set the header on `init.headers`, it wins — explicit\n * intent beats ambient context.\n */\nexport async function runtimeFetch(path, init = {}) {\n  const url = joinPath(activeRuntimePrefix(), path);\n  const headers = new Headers(init.headers || {});\n\n  // The scope header is belt-and-suspenders: the agent-path proxy strips and\n  // re-asserts it server-side. We still send it so audit logs and a\n  // not-yet-upgraded proxy both see the intended scope.\n  if (_activeAgentScope && !headers.has(AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER)) {\n    headers.set(AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER, _activeAgentScope);\n  }\n\n  const response = await fetch(url, {\n    ...init,\n    headers,\n    credentials: init.credentials || \"same-origin\"\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const body = await readErrorDetail(response);\n    throw createRuntimeError(response, body);\n  }\n\n  return response;\n}\n\n/**\n * Same as runtimeFetch, but injects the X-Benny-Agent-Scope header\n * unconditionally. Default scope is \"sandbox\" (writes confined to\n * agent_sandbox/). Pass {scope:\"read_only\"} to disallow writes entirely.\n *\n * Agent-authored writes that target anything outside /api/runtime/agent_sandbox/\n * will be rejected by the runtime with HTTP 403.\n */\nexport async function fetchAsAgent(path, init = {}, options = {}) {\n  const scope = options.scope || \"sandbox\";\n  validateScope(scope);\n\n  const headers = new Headers(init.headers || {});\n  headers.set(AGENT_SCOPE_HEADER, scope);\n\n  // Run inside the agent scope context so runtimeFetch routes to the\n  // agent-runtime facade (and not the trusted human path) for this call.\n  return withAgentScope(scope, () => runtimeFetch(path, { ...init, headers }));\n}\n\nexport async function readRuntimeJson(response) {\n  const text = await response.text();\n  return text ? JSON.parse(text) : null;\n}\n\n/**\n * Convenience: GET /api/runtime/widgets and parse the JSON body. Throws\n * RuntimeError if the runtime is unreachable or returns non-2xx.\n *\n * When called from an agent context (withAgentScope or\n * createAgentRuntimeClient), the listing fetch is itself tagged with the\n * agent scope header so the audit log records who asked.\n */\nexport async function listWidgets() {\n  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/widgets\");\n  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n}\n\n/**\n * Phase D3 — save a JSON layout view into the workspace's\n * `agent_sandbox/views/` subtree.\n *\n * The runtime endpoint validates that the body parses as JSON and forces\n * `subdir=\"views\"` so a stray call cannot silently land in `drafts/` or\n * `notes/`. Callers may pass either a JSON string or any JSON-serialisable\n * object — objects are stringified before send so the JSON validation on\n * both sides agrees.\n *\n * Filename convention: `<id>.aamp.view`, but enforcement happens server-side\n * (no path separators, no leading dot). This helper does not invent the\n * extension — Phase F .aamp.view signing belongs at the manifest layer, not\n * here.\n *\n * Returns the runtime's `SandboxWriteResponse`:\n *   { status: \"written\", workspace, relative_path, bytes_written }\n *\n * Auto-injects the active agent scope when one is set; the bound-client\n * variant forces it. Without scope this is a human-driven write — the runtime\n * still validates JSON and path containment.\n *\n * @param {string} workspace\n * @param {string} filename\n * @param {string | object} content\n * @param {{ agentId?: string }} [options]\n * @returns {Promise<{status: \"written\", workspace: string, relative_path: string, bytes_written: number}>}\n */\nexport async function saveView(workspace, filename, content, options = {}) {\n  const body = serialiseViewContent(content);\n  const payload = {\n    workspace,\n    subdir: \"views\",\n    filename,\n    content: body,\n    agent_id: options.agentId || \"anonymous_agent\"\n  };\n  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/agent_sandbox/views/save\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify(payload)\n  });\n  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n}\n\n/**\n * Phase D3 — load a saved view from `agent_sandbox/views/`.\n *\n * Returns the runtime's read envelope:\n *   { workspace, subdir: \"views\", filename, relative_path, content, bytes }\n *\n * `content` is the raw UTF-8 string the file contains. By default the helper\n * also parses it as JSON and exposes the result on the `view` property —\n * pass `{ parseJson: false }` to skip parsing for non-JSON layouts (none\n * exist today; the runtime guards JSON on save, but the read endpoint is\n * format-agnostic).\n *\n * @param {string} workspace\n * @param {string} filename\n * @param {{ parseJson?: boolean }} [options]\n */\nexport async function loadView(workspace, filename, options = {}) {\n  const path = `/agent_sandbox/read/${encodeURIComponent(workspace)}/views/${encodeURIComponent(filename)}`;\n  const response = await runtimeFetch(path);\n  const envelope = await readRuntimeJson(response);\n  const parseJson = options.parseJson !== false;\n  if (parseJson && envelope && typeof envelope.content === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      envelope.view = JSON.parse(envelope.content);\n    } catch (err) {\n      const error = new Error(`loadView: stored content is not valid JSON: ${err.message}`);\n      error.name = \"RuntimeError\";\n      error.cause = err;\n      throw error;\n    }\n  }\n  return envelope;\n}\n\n/**\n * Phase D3 — list saved view filenames for a workspace.\n *\n * Returns the entries array directly (the runtime envelope's `entries` field).\n * Pass `{ raw: true }` to get the full envelope `{ workspace, subdir, entries }`\n * instead.\n *\n * @param {string} workspace\n * @param {{ raw?: boolean }} [options]\n */\nexport async function listViews(workspace, options = {}) {\n  const path = `/agent_sandbox/list/${encodeURIComponent(workspace)}/views`;\n  const response = await runtimeFetch(path);\n  const envelope = await readRuntimeJson(response);\n  if (options.raw) {\n    return envelope;\n  }\n  return envelope && Array.isArray(envelope.entries) ? envelope.entries : [];\n}\n\n/**\n * Phase F — sign a `.aamp.view` layout via the runtime's HMAC chokepoint.\n *\n * Posts the view to `/api/views/sign` (intentionally outside the agent_sandbox\n * prefix). `AgentScopeMiddleware` blocks any agent-scoped POST here with HTTP\n * 403, so calling `signView` from a bound agent client surfaces the security\n * boundary as a `RuntimeError(status=403)` — the runtime is the enforcer, not\n * this module.\n *\n * Accepts a JSON-serialisable view object. The runtime computes HMAC-SHA256\n * over a canonical payload (sorted keys, no whitespace, `signature` field\n * stripped) and returns:\n *\n *   { signature: { algorithm, value, signed_at }, canonical_payload: \"...\" }\n *\n * The canonical payload is returned so callers can audit exactly what was\n * signed before embedding the signature back into the view.\n *\n * @param {object} view\n * @param {{ }} [options]\n * @returns {Promise<{signature: {algorithm: string, value: string, signed_at: string}, canonical_payload: string}>}\n */\nexport async function signView(view, options = {}) {\n  if (!view || typeof view !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(view)) {\n    throw new Error(\"signView: view must be a JSON object.\");\n  }\n  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/views/sign\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ view })\n  });\n  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n}\n\n/**\n * Phase F — verify an HMAC-SHA256 signature over a `.aamp.view` payload.\n *\n * Posts `{view, signature}` to `/api/views/verify` and returns the runtime's\n * boolean result. The runtime uses `hmac.compare_digest` to avoid timing\n * leaks; clients must treat any non-true result as a verification failure.\n *\n * Like `signView`, this endpoint sits outside `/api/agent_sandbox/`, so a\n * bound agent client invoking it triggers the middleware's 403 — verification\n * is a human / shell-server action.\n *\n * @param {object} view\n * @param {{algorithm: string, value: string, signed_at: string}} signature\n * @param {{ }} [options]\n * @returns {Promise<boolean>}\n */\nexport async function verifyView(view, signature, options = {}) {\n  if (!view || typeof view !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(view)) {\n    throw new Error(\"verifyView: view must be a JSON object.\");\n  }\n  if (!signature || typeof signature !== \"object\") {\n    throw new Error(\"verifyView: signature must be an envelope object.\");\n  }\n  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/views/verify\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ view, signature })\n  });\n  const body = await readRuntimeJson(response);\n  return Boolean(body && body.valid);\n}\n\n/**\n * Phase F2 — promote an agent-drafted view to a signed, canonical workspace\n * location.\n *\n * Posts `{workspace, source_filename, target_filename?, pinned_by?}` to\n * `/api/views/pin`. The runtime re-reads the draft from\n * `agent_sandbox/views/<source_filename>`, signs it, embeds the signature\n * inline, writes to `<workspace>/views/<target_filename>` (defaulting to\n * `source_filename`), and emits a `VIEW_PINNED` audit event.\n *\n * Same human-only boundary as `signView` — `/api/views/pin` lives outside\n * `/api/agent_sandbox/`, so a bound agent client invoking this triggers\n * `RuntimeError(status=403)`.\n *\n * Returns the runtime's `PinViewResponse`:\n *   {\n *     workspace, source_relative_path, pinned_relative_path,\n *     bytes_written, signature: { algorithm, value, signed_at }\n *   }\n *\n * @param {string} workspace\n * @param {string} sourceFilename — must match `agent_sandbox/views/<filename>`\n * @param {{ targetFilename?: string, pinnedBy?: string }} [options]\n */\nexport async function pinView(workspace, sourceFilename, options = {}) {\n  if (typeof workspace !== \"string\" || !workspace) {\n    throw new Error(\"pinView: workspace is required.\");\n  }\n  if (typeof sourceFilename !== \"string\" || !sourceFilename) {\n    throw new Error(\"pinView: sourceFilename is required.\");\n  }\n  const payload = {\n    workspace,\n    source_filename: sourceFilename\n  };\n  if (options.targetFilename) {\n    payload.target_filename = options.targetFilename;\n  }\n  if (options.pinnedBy) {\n    payload.pinned_by = options.pinnedBy;\n  }\n  const response = await runtimeFetch(\"/views/pin\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify(payload)\n  });\n  return readRuntimeJson(response);\n}\n\n/**\n * Phase F2b — read a pinned view AND verify its embedded signature in one\n * round-trip.\n *\n * GETs ``/api/views/load/<workspace>/<filename>``. The runtime reads\n * ``$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/<ws>/views/<filename>``, extracts the\n * ``signature`` field embedded by ``pinView``, recomputes the HMAC against\n * the rest of the canonical payload, and returns:\n *\n *   {\n *     workspace, filename, relative_path, bytes,\n *     view: { …, signature: {algorithm, value, signed_at} },\n *     signature: { algorithm, value, signed_at } | null,\n *     valid: boolean\n *   }\n *\n * ``valid: false`` is NOT an HTTP error — the caller is expected to branch\n * on it. A missing or malformed inline signature surfaces as ``valid: false``\n * with ``signature: null``; structural problems (no such file, body is not\n * JSON, body is not an object) surface as HTTP 404 / 400.\n *\n * Reads are unrestricted by ``AgentScopeMiddleware`` so this works from any\n * caller — human, bound agent client, or anonymous shell. The runtime is\n